implementationPlan.description:
Fake-daemon support in scripts/tests/postflight-fake-proxy.js. This is test infrastructure and stays inert unless used.
(a) get_context: FAKE_CTX_CONTRACT=<JSON object> is served as task.executionContract on the task-scoped read. Put it in the switch's get_context case, beside FAKE_CTX_WORKSPACE and FAKE_CTX_COMMITS, mirroring tools/getContext.ts, which serves the field only when set. Parse it with jsonKnob; a non-object throws, as FAKE_CTX_LANDING does. Unset means no field, so today's payload is unchanged.
(b) candidateReply: when args.protectedEntries is present, refuse it unless it obeys packages/moe-daemon/src/state/candidateStore.ts readProtectedEntries:
- an array of at most 2000 entries;
- each entry a plain object whose only keys are path and oid;
- path equal to its own util/affectedFiles.ts normalization: trimmed, no backslash, no leading '/' or './', no empty, '.' or '..' segment, at most 500 chars, and no control character (0x00-0x1f, 0x7f);
- oid matching /^[0-9a-f]{40}$/;
- paths strictly ascending by Buffer.compare.
Absent stays absent, and the echoed candidate carries the list exactly as sent, so the wrapper's acknowledgement compares it. Document both knobs in the header notes.
Error handling: each violation throws a plain Error naming the rule inside evidenceRpc's try. The wrapper then sees the FIXTURE_REFUSED refusal it already handles, and the row fails on a refused record instead of a fixture crash. Nothing else changes, so suites that never send protectedEntries (the postflight.{sh,ps1} frozen modes, postflight-worktree.cjs, the other vm-route sections) see identical replies. The rows of steps 2-3 and the sort mutant of step 5 test this validator.

Adversarial self-review (load adversarial-self-review) of the whole diff, then prove the rows bite.
Run each mutant in a scratch snapshot on /mnt/d (never in W, never with sed -i on tracked files), using the fast slices from mem:pattern-vm-route-strong-receipt-slice. Each mutant must turn its row red, in both wrappers:
1. Drop the strong gate, so the field is sent for any task with requiredChecks. Red row: SG-legacy.
2. Measure the base tree instead of FROZEN_TREE / $Frozen.Tree. Red row: PE-pass (vm-job.txt).
3. Sort case-insensitively (sh key=str.lower; ps1 Sort-Object). Red row: PE-pass, and the fake refuses the unsorted list.
4. Call ls-tree without a pathspec for an empty path list. Red row: PE-empty.
5. Skip non-blob records instead of omitting the field. Red row: PE-unmeasured.
Also check:
- legacy and observe add no git call, context parse or output line;
- nothing reads an env var, setting or CLI-writable file to decide strong or the paths (task rails);
- the [WARN] bytes match across the wrappers;
- the ps1 BOM is intact;
- the frozen-mode payloads are unchanged;
- no existing test assertion was weakened.
List the mutants and their red rows in the completion summary. If this review changes any byte, re-run checkRefs[0] and submit that fresh run.
